Well, so much for omega.  I'm back to playing nethack again, wands
of death and all.  No willpower :-)  Damn, this game's addictive!

In article <ABRAHAM.93May21013458@loke.iesd.auc.dk>, abraham@research.att.com (Per Abrahamsen) writes:
> 
> Here are a number of easy to implement suggestions, that would make
> nethack easier for beginners and low-levels characters, and more
> difficult for experienced players and high-level characters.
> 
> - Let wands of polymorph use one charge for each item or monster being
> polymorphed.

Hmmm... not sure about this one.  I guess it'd work, since I hardly ever
polypile anyway.

> - Let intrinsic protections have a (long) time-out.

Good idea.

> - Remove wands of wishing from the game.  Replace the wand with a
> magic lamp in the castle level. 

I disagree here.  Sure, it's possible to get 8 or 9 wishes in a game,
but it doesn't happen often.  And you need that WoW in the castle to
get those items you simply haven't been able to find, like blessed 
tinning kits etc.
  
> - Make it impossible to wish for named weapons.

No.  It's already difficult to wish for artifacts when you've already 
got more than one.  I'd suggest making the penalty for using a non-
aligned artifact much higher, though - perhaps it should force your 
alignment to shift, generally peeving your God.  Plus, of course,
causing *lots* of damage when you first use it (like 50-100HP?)

> - Make it impossible to get a named weapon from the Gods.

Again, no.  You *need* a named weapon to finish the game.

> - Give the priest in Gehennom a named weapon, so the player have one
> in Hell.

Yeah, why not?

> - Make intelligent monsters immune to conflict.

Yep, good idea.

> - Restrict wand zapping to high-level monsters, especially the more
> deadly wands.  A Gnome Lord should be allowed to zap magic missiles.

Yes!  Now, this is the best idea I've heard yet as regards wands.  But
the getting zapped by a wand of sleep timeout needs to be reduced.  As
for wands of death, well, I guess they're rare enough.

> - Make being killed when polymorphed lower your CON attribute, and if
> it is too low (< 5) you die for real.

Yes.  And make that a permanent loss, i.e. not recoverable with a unicorn
horn.  The only way to regain it would be exercise and gain ability.  But
make the lower limit 3.
 
> - Make food consumption lower, but let high stats and/or intrinsic
> raise it.

Hmmm.  Dunno.

> - Make regeneration faster for low level characters, and slower for
> high-level characters compared to now.  

Yeah, that might not be a bad idea.
 
> - A chrysknife should be significantly better than all other non-named
> weapons.

The crysknife's a bit of legacy, isn't it?  A throwback to the days of
hack 1.0 (yeah, I used to play that :), when the crysknife was by far 
the best weapon you could get.

> - If maxhp is over 100, it should very slowly decrease.  Carrying
> Yendor could raise this to 150.

Hmmm.

> - Players should be forced to drop all all items that do not fit the
> players character class when entering the endgame.

Yes.

> What do you think?

Some good suggestions there.

